{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If</b> … <b>and My testimonies</b> — [the word] has a holeam in place of a shureq, or it is a strange hybrid word composed of singular and plural forms, like <b>והפלא ה' את מכותך</b> ('and HaShem will inflict extraordinary blows upon you'). The mem of <b>אלמדם</b> ['I will instruct them'] is in <b>אל בריתי ועדותי</b>, and likewise the word <b>גם הם ישבו גם בניהם</b> ['they sat, their children too']."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 132, :notes {0 "The reference to holeam/shureq concerns the word עדותי in the verse; the precise grammatical argument is compressed and the comparison to the other cited verses is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:37.541947323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}